{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xcgpj5vq4kwdfnhdffzmahw35ol3i2f2sb4qdk7kj4ha5v52lpdq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases done, all gates green.\n\n## What I found\n\nThe library is a single translation unit with a single public function:\n\n```c\nvoid driver(int x) { register int y = 2*x; y += 300; printf(\"%d\\n\", y); }\n```\n\n**No divergences were found — the Rust translation in `src/lib.rs` needed no fixes.** It correctly reproduces the C's de-facto two's-complement wrapping (confirmed against the C's own disassembly: `lea (%rax,%rax,1),%ebx; add $0x12c,%ebx`, all 32-bit) and calls libc `printf` directly so the byte stream is identical.\n\n## Phase A — surface map (artifacts in crate root)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` for both `.so`s. C exports exactly 1 defined dynamic symbol (`driver`); Rust exports the same. Symbol diff is **empty**. All Rust undefined symbols are libc/libgcc only (`ldd` resolves everything). Both are `FUNC GLOBAL DEFAULT`. Also records that the whole C inventory (1 file, 1 function) is translated — nothing skipped, nothing stubbed. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 11 rows. A mechanical grep for `return/assert/NULL/if/switch/#ifdef/ERROR/exit/abort/comparisons` over the entire C source yields **exactly one hit** (`#include <stdio.h>`): the library has zero error paths, zero pointer/length/enum parameters. The table therefore enumerates the real boundary surface: `INT_MAX`, `INT_MIN`, first multiply-overflow on each side, the `y += 300` overflow edge, all-bit-patterns (the out-of-range-enum analogue), 64-bit-register upper-bit truncation, zero, and printf-write failure. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 21 rows. No runtime options/flags/`#ifdef` modes exist, so the axes are input shape (sign, overflow class of each of the two arithmetic ops, output sign/decimal width 1–10 digits) × call-sequence shape (zero/one/many/repeated/interleaved C↔Rust, pipe vs file buffering, non-main thread, large batches). |\n\n**Feature combinations:** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table and `CMakeLists.txt` has no options/defines → the complete space is `{}` (== default). Verified via a script that parses `Cargo.toml` and loops over the cross-product.\n\n## Phases B–D — tests\n\n`tests/differential.rs` (34 tests) loads **both** `.so`s with `libloading` (`RTLD_LOCAL`, so the two identically-named `driver` symbols can't shadow each other) and only ever calls the exported symbol — so the `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is under test. Since the sole observable effect is stdout, each test redirects fd 1, runs the same sequence against each library, and compares bytes. Inputs are property-style randomized from a fixed-seed PCG-XSH-RR, plus a 200 000-value contiguous sweep and a stride-65 521 sweep covering the whole `i32` domain.\n\nOne harness bug I hit and fixed: with libtest's default parallelism, its own progress lines leak into the captured fd 1 (false divergences). Captures now validate that the bytes contain only `-?[0-9]+\\n` and retry otherwise, so `cargo test` passes both parallel and with `--test-threads=1`.\n\n`./verify.sh` runs the whole gate: C cmake build → per-feature-combo `cargo check`/`build` → `nm -D` diff → tests; then the default-features invocation, a parallel run, and the release profile (`panic = \"abort\"`) `.so`. Result: **34/34 passing in every configuration, symbols identical, `ALL VERIFICATION STEPS PASSED`**. `Cargo.toml` gained only `libloading = \"0.8\"` under `[dev-dependencies]`; nothing in `c_src/` was modified (only the generated `build/` directory added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1628,"cache_read_input_tokens":91212,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1628,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,